"82_number_math.mst — MACDART: raisedTo: for EVERY exponent.

 51_number_ext's raisedTo: (kept verbatim there) supports only integer
 exponents and signals on anything else — so `2 raisedTo: 0.5` errored where
 every Smalltalk answers sqrt 2. This overlay re-points it at dart:cocoa's
 stRaisedTo: integer exponents stay EXACT (an int base promotes through the
 bignum tower; a Fraction accumulates via its own *; a negative exponent
 answers the exact reciprocal — a Fraction for an int base), and a fractional
 exponent goes through doubles (math.pow). 51's `**` delegates to raisedTo:,
 so it inherits all of this. Loads after 51 (file 82); reopen replaces."

Number >> raisedTo: aNumber [ <stprim: stRaisedTo> ]
